    "created_at": "2026-03-12T13:44:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-12T13:44:13Z",
    "body": "`window.stop` also has this interaction. Per spec, calling `window.stop` will not abort an ongoing navigate event fired from [#navigate-fragid](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-fragid). I think Blink does though, whereas Gecko does not. This only became apparent in Gecko after implementing #12256.\n\nThe fix mentioned above does not cover all cases. It's not clear if `document.open`/`window.stop` should be able to abort ongoing \"traverse\" navigations, but spec definitely says that that should be impossible. Because the other \"easy\" fix would be to make fragment navigations set ongoing navigation, but it's not entirely clear to me what the effect would be.\n\n@noamr do you have any insights to this?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
